<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Caterpillar '98 estimate raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Caterpillar '98 estimate raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- For the first six months of 1997, the construction and mining equipment  maker reported earnings of $2.19 a share.</p>
<p>-- The rating change came after New Holland NV management said in  a conference call that there had been a stabilization in the European  construction market with an anticipated rebound in 1998, Smith Barney  said.</p>
<p>-- Caterpillar would be a key beneficiary of improvement in European  construction equipment demand, Smith Barney said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
